Z||000002||Ed||06-08-2000||11:08 PM||||My solution was to take my car to the local Chevy dealer.  <P>While they had the engine out I had them replace all the rubber parts which could or had fail(ed), and a bunch of other stuff to "restore" the car to the best possible state. <P>Of course it cost a lot of money, but it was "easy" and "simple." <P>P.S. I just read, "Mad at my Fiero too."  That's why the dealer does most of my work now!  <P>[This message has been edited by Ed (edited 06-08-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Ed (edited 06-08-2000).]||||reg||1
